From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wu Yuwei <yuweiwu@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 03:08:33 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Walk a glyph run's clusters from its span

An embedder that keeps a line's glyph runs as spans of the shaped text
(GlyphSpan) also needs their clusters, for selection, hit testing and
text-overflow, but only for the few runs those ask about: copying them
out of every run each time the lines are broken is most of the work.

GlyphSpan::clusters gives the clusters Run::visual_clusters gives of the
glyph run's style on its line (with or without glyphs: a newline's too),
their text and their advance with the line's spacing, from the shaped
text alone. The span keeps the run's clusters on the line and the style
for it. Run's Clusters and GlyphSpan::clusters walk the same graphemes
with their atoms (AtomGraphemes, taken out of Clusters), so the spacing
is worked out once.

GlyphSpan::text_range gives where those clusters' text starts (the
visually first) and how far it reaches, from the characters alone, for
an embedder that maps a run to its source text as it lays it out.
